CORE
main.c
--pointer-check
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.pointer_dereference\.\d+\] line 19 .*pointer NULL in \*p: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^\[main\.pointer_dereference\.\d+\] line 19 .*pointer NULL in \*p: SUCCESS$
--
A function call that takes the address of a local pointer (clobber(&p)) can
change that pointer's value, so cached pointer-validity assertions about the
local must be cleared at the call. Without that, the NULL dereference at line
19 is deduplicated against the cached check from line 14 and silently dropped,
and verification wrongly succeeds.
